(Cell Membranes - Study Notes) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The fluid mosaic model) Tj T*
(The cell membrane is a phospholipid bilayer. Each phospholipid has a) Tj T*
(hydrophilic \(water-loving\) head and two hydrophobic \(water-fearing\) tails.) Tj T*
(In water, the tails hide inside while the heads face outward. Proteins float) Tj T*
(in this bilayer like icebergs, which is why it is called a mosaic.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Membrane proteins) Tj T*
(Integral proteins span the whole bilayer and act as channels or carriers.) Tj T*
(Peripheral proteins sit on the surface and work as enzymes or signals.) Tj T*
(Carbohydrate chains attached to proteins form the glycocalyx, used for) Tj T*
(cell recognition.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Selective permeability) Tj T*
(Small nonpolar molecules \(O2, CO2\) diffuse freely across. Ions and large) Tj T*
(polar molecules need transport proteins. Osmosis is the diffusion of water) Tj T*
(across a selectively permeable membrane, from low to high solute concentration.) Tj T*
ET
